    silm:hasLongDescription "The MereologyDiagram is the part-whole diagram of Mittens-the-cat, indexed by body-region tags (head, torso, paws, tail) and overlap joints. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'D_Mittens', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

silm:instances_papers_19_mereology_as_colimit_chapters_03_per_leg_profile_top_level_sections_01_per_leg_mereology_profile_concrete_anchor
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "PerLegMereologyProfileConcreteAnchorExample" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'PerLegMereologyProfileConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, the head-region olog fragment of Mittens's vet exam: left ear position, right ear position, three-color torbie eye markings; also, the clinical care plan record 77 generated for Mittens at the May 2026 vet visit at the Tartu Animal Clinic; also, the Felis catus taxon node, TSN 183798, kept as a typed leg origin distinct from the apex Mittens-the-cat." .

