silm:instances_papers_19_mereology_as_colimit_chapters_06_pushout_and_coequalizer_zoo_sections_03_indexing_category_diagrams_concrete_anchor%23homfunctor
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.19_mereology_as_colimit.chapters.06_pushout_and_coequalizer_zoo.sections.03_indexing_category_diagrams.concrete_anchor#homfunctor" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The HomFunctor is the hom-functor Hom_C(-, X) that takes any probe object and asks what arrows from it land in X under the category C. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Hom', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

silm:instances_papers_19_mereology_as_colimit_chapters_06_pushout_and_coequalizer_zoo_sections_03_indexing_category_diagrams_concrete_anchor%23setcategory
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.19_mereology_as_colimit.chapters.06_pushout_and_coequalizer_zoo.sections.03_indexing_category_diagrams.concrete_anchor#setcategory" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The SetCategory is the category of sets and functions, the target of every representable presheaf in the Yoneda embedding of C. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Set', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

silm:instances_papers_19_mereology_as_colimit_chapters_06_pushout_and_coequalizer_zoo_sections_03_indexing_category_diagrams_concrete_anchor%23categoryofcategories
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.19_mereology_as_colimit.chapters.06_pushout_and_coequalizer_zoo.sections.03_indexing_category_diagrams.concrete_anchor#categoryofcategories" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The CategoryOfCategories is the 2-category of categories whose objects are categories and whose 1-arrows are functors between them. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Cat', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

silm:instances_papers_19_mereology_as_colimit_chapters_06_pushout_and_coequalizer_zoo_sections_03_indexing_category_diagrams_concrete_anchor%23sheafcondition
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.19_mereology_as_colimit.chapters.06_pushout_and_coequalizer_zoo.sections.03_indexing_category_diagrams.concrete_anchor#sheafcondition" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The SheafCondition is the sheaf-condition gluing law for typed leg observations across overlap covers in the J_Mittens index category. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Sheaf', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

silm:instances_papers_19_mereology_as_colimit_chapters_06_pushout_and_coequalizer_zoo_sections_03_indexing_category_diagrams_concrete_anchor%23kanextension
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.19_mereology_as_colimit.chapters.06_pushout_and_coequalizer_zoo.sections.03_indexing_category_diagrams.concrete_anchor#kanextension" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The KanExtension is the Kan extension construction lifting partial cocones along a functor, used in the cross-paper bridge to paper 27. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Kan', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

