    silm:hasLongDescription "The LegOriginFunctor is the functor that picks out the origin object of a named cocone leg in the D_Mittens diagram (head, torso, evidence, role). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'LegOrigin', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

silm:instances_papers_19_mereology_as_colimit_chapters_02_sources_and_closure_sections_04_joy_of_cats_clause_unpacking_concrete_anchor%23legcoconearrow
